New Feature: WhatsApp Notification to YOU on Every Booking
What changed
File	What changed
notifications.py	Added send_owner_whatsapp_notification() — sends a WhatsApp message to your number whenever a customer books
app.py	Calls it right after a booking is saved (/api/book)
.env.example	Added TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM and OWNER_WHATSAPP_NUMBER

This is separate from the customer-facing WhatsApp button (that one is just a link, no setup needed). This new one is a real automated message that lands in your WhatsApp whenever someone books — needs Twilio.

Why WhatsApp Sandbox instead of the SMS route

The SMS setup earlier got stuck on India phone number compliance (KYC documents). WhatsApp Sandbox skips all of that — it's meant for exactly this: notifying yourself, not messaging random customers. Free, works immediately.

Limitation: sandbox messages only reach numbers that have joined the sandbox (i.e., you — one-time step below). This is fine since only you need to receive these.

Setup Steps
1. Join the Twilio WhatsApp Sandbox (one-time, on your phone)
Go to Twilio Console → search "Try it out" or "WhatsApp" in the left sidebar → "Send a WhatsApp message" / "Sandbox settings".
It'll show a WhatsApp number (+1 415 523 8886) and a join code like join <two-words>.
On your phone, open WhatsApp and send that exact join <code> message to that number.
You'll get a confirmation reply — you're now connected to the sandbox.
2. Add Environment Variables on Render

Render dashboard → ac-oscar service → Environment:

Key	Value
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID	(same one from earlier SMS setup)
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN	(same one from earlier SMS setup)
OWNER_WHATSAPP_NUMBER	your number, e.g. 9150821143
TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM	whatsapp:+14155238886 (leave as default — this is Twilio's sandbox number, not something you buy)

You do not need TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER for this feature (that one's only for the customer SMS feature, which is separate and still optional).

3. Save → Render redeploys automatically
4. Test

Make a test booking on your site → within a few seconds you should get a WhatsApp message on your phone with the booking details (tracking code, customer name, phone, AC type, issue, preferred slot).

Note on the Sandbox
The sandbox is free and has no message limit for testing, but Twilio may require you to re-join every ~72 hours of inactivity (they'll remind you if so).
If you later want a permanent, always-on WhatsApp sender for your business (not just a sandbox), that requires WhatsApp Business API approval through Twilio — a longer process with its own verification. Not needed for just notifying yourself; only relevant if you also want to message customers on WhatsApp automatically in the future.
